-- title:
--   Norm conjugator identifies centralizer with twisted centralizer
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be fields with $L$ a finite-dimensional Galois extension of $K$, and let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup of integral powers of $\sigma$ (so $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$). Let $A$ be a commutative topological ring which is a $K$-algebra, and give $L \otimes_K A$ the topology coming from the scoped right-action tensor instances, so that $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K A)$ is a topological group. Let $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(A)$ satisfy [`AutomorphicForm.IsRegularSemisimple`](def/AutomorphicForm_LocalOrbitalBase.html#L402), i.e. $\operatorname{tr}(\gamma)^2 - 4\det(\gamma)$ is a unit of $A$, and let $\delta, y \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K A)$ satisfy [`AutomorphicForm.IsNormConjugator`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L214), i.e.
--   $$\iota(\gamma) = y^{-1}\,\bigl(\textstyle\prod_{i=0}^{n-1}\sigma^i(\delta)\bigr)\, y, \qquad n = [L:K],$$
--   where $\iota =$ [`AutomorphicForm.toTensorGL`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L71) is the map $\mathrm{GL}_2(A) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K A)$ induced entrywise by $a \mapsto 1 \otimes a$, and $\sigma$ acts on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K A)$ entrywise through the first tensor factor. Then there is an isomorphism of topological groups $e$ (a group isomorphism which is simultaneously a homeomorphism) from the centralizer of $\gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(A)$ onto the twisted centralizer $\{t : t\,\delta\,\sigma(t)^{-1} = \delta\}$ of $\delta$, both with their subspace topologies, such that $e(s) = y\,\iota(s)\,y^{-1}$ for every $s$ in the centralizer of $\gamma$.
--
--   This is the statement that the $\sigma$-twisted centralizer of $\delta$ is, over the base, identified with the centralizer of a norm of $\delta$ by means of any norm conjugator — the group-theoretic input for matching twisted and ordinary orbital integrals in cyclic base change for $\mathrm{GL}_2$. It is used downstream in the comparison of twisted and ordinary orbital data, including the statements about coupled families over the adele ring and the elliptic families attached to twisted centralizers.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_exists_continuousMulEquiv_centralizer_twistedCentralizer_of_isNormConjugator.lean

